WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.135 --> 00:00:09.202
Jackie tried not to worry as her black Labrador retriever, Poke, walked beside her into the

2
00:00:09.203 --> 00:00:18.783
show ring. The ring was a square grassy area surrounded by a low fence. Poke

3
00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:26.195
loved performing in dog shows, but he had a mischievous streak. And right now his eyes

4
00:00:26.196 --> 00:00:31.432
were sparkling with a familiar look. It said, "Watch this!" "Stay," Jackie told Poke as

5
00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:37.359
they reached their spot in the ring. Poke froze like a statue, but Jackie did not

6
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.513
take her attention away from him. The seven other handlers entered the ring with their

7
00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:55.267
dogs. They lined up according to the size of their dogs, from biggest to smallest. A

8
00:00:55.268 --> 00:01:02.821
girl named Priscilla entered last with a small dog named Fluffy. Jackie lightly touched Poke's

9
00:01:02.822 --> 00:01:09.560
chin. He lifted his head slightly, not moving the rest of his body. Only his eyes

10
00:01:09.561 --> 00:01:13.661
danced. Poke loved to show off as much as Jackie loved showing him. "Please take your

11
00:01:13.662 --> 00:01:23.574
dogs around," the judge said. "Go," Jackie said to Poke. The two of them led

12
00:01:23.575 --> 00:01:30.065
the way, trotting in a circle with the other dogs and handlers following. Spectators sat in

13
00:01:30.066 --> 00:01:34.229
folding chairs around the ring, including Jackie's friends and her grandmother. Grandma was the one

14
00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:38.464
who'd taught Jackie how to show dogs. "You've got this!" Jackie's friend Hudson called. Jackie kept

15
00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:44.478
her eyes on Poke. "I hope Hudson is right," she thought. All year she had

16
00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:53.186
watched her friends move up from the novice class for beginners to the open class for

17
00:01:53.187 --> 00:01:59.859
more experienced handlers. Jackie had felt left behind. But if she won this show, she

18
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:06.786
could move up too! Once the dogs were lined up again, the judge turned to Jackie.

19
00:02:06.787 --> 00:02:13.022
"Bring him up," she said. "Please be good, Poke," Jackie muttered as Poke heeled at her

20
00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:16.512
side. "Take him around the ring," the judge said. "Go." Jackie broke into a run

21
00:02:16.513 --> 00:02:24.836
on the right side of the dog, holding the leash. Poke trotted slightly ahead of her

22
00:02:24.837 --> 00:02:32.671
around the ring. Jackie kept a steady pace to show off Poke's best gait. "Up

23
00:02:32.672 --> 00:02:42.498
and back," the judge said. Jackie and Poke trotted to the far side of the ring

24
00:02:42.499 --> 00:02:49.903
and back. Next, Jackie stacked the dog. This meant putting Poke in the best standing

25
00:02:49.904 --> 00:02:56.658
position to show him off. She touched the dog's elbow so he'd move his front feet

26
00:02:56.659 --> 00:03:01.234
slightly forward, stretching out his body. The judge walked around Poke, her expression serious. Jackie

27
00:03:01.235 --> 00:03:11.783
knew exactly what the judge was looking for. The American Kennel Club had a breed standard

28
00:03:11.784 --> 00:03:16.362
for every breed of dog. These standards defined the best traits of each breed. Poke was

29
00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:24.623
a champion—that meant he came close to what the AKC considered a perfect Labrador retriever.

30
00:03:24.624 --> 00:03:30.868
At this show, however, Poke wasn't being judged. Jackie was. This show was for junior handlers,

31
00:03:30.869 --> 00:03:37.040
a competition for kids learning to show dogs. Junior handler shows judged the handler's knowledge

32
00:03:37.041 --> 00:03:44.112
of her breed and the rules and etiquette of the ring. The judge knelt in front

33
00:03:44.113 --> 00:03:53.401
of Poke. She studied his broad head. She pulled back Poke's lips to look at

34
00:03:53.402 --> 00:04:00.519
his teeth. The tip of Poke's tail quivered. "Stand still," Jackie whispered. Poke's tail stopped moving.

35
00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:06.683
"Perfect," Jackie thought. She felt a thrill. Their turn was almost over, and she hadn't made

36
00:04:06.684 --> 00:04:11.817
a single mistake! Then it happened. Jackie felt a slight movement on the leash .

37
00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:23.423
. . and Poke leaned forward and slathered the judge's face with his tongue! "Oh no!"

38
00:04:23.424 --> 00:04:33.061
Jackie thought, but she stayed calm. She gave a gentle tug on the leash to

39
00:04:33.062 --> 00:04:39.399
bring Poke back into position. Poke obeyed, his mouth open in a big grin. "He's certainly

40
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:45.535
friendly." The judge wiped her face with a tissue. Jackie nodded with a polite smile.

41
00:04:45.536 --> 00:04:55.965
She could feel that her own face was still beet red as she walked Poke toward

42
00:04:55.966 --> 00:04:59.962
the back of the line. "Tough break," Priscilla whispered. Jackie couldn't meet her eyes. She

43
00:04:59.963 --> 00:05:04.635
felt humiliated. The secret to handling a dog was staying in control so the dog would

44
00:05:04.636 --> 00:05:14.621
look its best. And she had just lost control of Poke. Poke nudged her leg with

45
00:05:14.622 --> 00:05:23.035
his nose. "You're not expecting a treat after that stunt, are you?" Jackie muttered. Keeping

46
00:05:23.036 --> 00:05:29.351
a firm hold on Poke, Jackie watched as the rest of the handlers went before the

47
00:05:29.352 --> 00:05:34.792
judge. This was a novice class, so half the kids didn't know what they were

48
00:05:34.793 --> 00:05:40.337
doing. A boy with a basset hound did okay, but he handled the dog too roughly.

49
00:05:40.338 --> 00:05:45.597
Jackie felt a trickle of hope. She needed a first-place finish today. But that depended

50
00:05:45.598 --> 00:05:55.092
on the other kids' performances. "We still have a chance, Poke," she muttered as Priscilla walked

51
00:05:55.093 --> 00:06:04.912
Fluffy to the judge. Priscilla was good. Jackie didn't see her make any mistakes—but Jackie

52
00:06:04.913 --> 00:06:17.242
didn't know anything about showing smaller dogs. The judge gave out the lower-place ribbons, and then

53
00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:22.240
walked toward Jackie and Priscilla, holding ribbons for first and second place. Jackie held her breath.

54
00:06:22.241 --> 00:06:28.978
"Nice job," the judge said, handing Jackie second place. "Your dog displays just the right

55
00:06:28.979 --> 00:06:34.985
temperament for the breed. He's friendly and willing to please. But you have to make sure

56
00:06:34.986 --> 00:06:43.707
he doesn't get the last word. He took control for a moment there." Jackie's heart

57
00:06:43.708 --> 00:06:48.950
plummeted, but she managed to hide her disappointment. "Thank you," she said, accepting the ribbon. The

58
00:06:48.951 --> 00:06:52.062
judge handed Priscilla the rose ribbon for first place. "Congratulations," Jackie said. "Thanks!" Priscilla was

59
00:06:52.063 --> 00:06:57.839
beaming. "It's my second win!" Jackie slowly walked Poke out of the ring. "You'll make it

60
00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:03.766
next time," Grandma said, giving her a hug. Grandma rubbed Poke's head. "I think Poke

61
00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:17.695
pulled that stunt because he knew it was his last show." "Last show?" Jackie felt the

62
00:07:17.696 --> 00:07:24.941
blood drain from her face. "What are you talking about, Grandma?" "Most show dogs are younger

63
00:07:24.942 --> 00:07:34.093
than five," Grandma said. "Poke's older, so I'm going to retire him." Tears filled Jackie's

64
00:07:34.094 --> 00:07:38.996
eyes as she hugged the big dog. She couldn't believe what she was hearing. "Why didn't

65
00:07:38.997 --> 00:07:46.661
you tell me, Grandma? I can't be in junior handlers without Poke!" Grandma patted Jackie's

66
00:07:46.662 --> 00:07:54.567
shoulder. "I didn't want to make you nervous or upset before today's event. And a skilled

67
00:07:54.568 --> 00:08:01.980
handler can show more than one dog—and more than one breed. You'll be fine." Jackie

68
00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:07.923
just shook her head. She knew what Grandma was saying was true. Plenty of kids changed

69
00:08:07.924 --> 00:08:12.740
dogs or worked with more than one. But Jackie had already been worried about advancing

70
00:08:12.741 --> 00:08:23.357
to open class. Now she was going to have to do it with a new dog!

